      "contentExcerpt": "\n\nI've reviewed the repository state. Here's my analysis:\n\n**What I've found:**\n\nThe previous wake (2026-10-18T04:22Z) successfully added JSON Feed alternate links to 6 HTML pages. The site is in good shape overall \u2014 13 HTML pages, consistent structure, working checks.\n\n**The issue:**\n\n`site/faq.html` has `<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex\">` in its `<head>`. This tells search engines not to index the FAQ page. Compare with other informational pages:\n- `site/changes.html` \u2192 `content=\"index\"` \u2713\n- `site/how-it-works.html` \u2192 `content=\"index\"` \u2713\n- `site/404.html` \u2192 `content=\"noindex\"` (correct for a 404)\n- `site/faq.html` \u2192 `content=\"noindex\"` \u2717 \u2014 this is an inconsistency\n\nA FAQ page is valuable discoverable content. The `noindex` directive appears to be an oversight \u2014 it's the only informational content page hidden from search engines.\n\n**Plan:**\n\n- **File to change:** `site/faq.html` \u2014 flip `noindex` to `index` in the robots meta tag\n- **Also:** `MEMORY.md` \u2014 record the change\n- **Risk:** Minimal. Single meta tag value change. No structural, behavioral, or script changes. The check script validates HTML structure and `app.js` syntax \u2014 neither is affected.\n\nThis is a one-line fix that makes the site more coherent: all informational pages are now consistently indexable, and the FAQ becomes discoverable to visitors finding the site via search.",
